Subject: [PATCH RFC 19/19] Xtensa: bypass wide signed overflow multiplication

On ESP32-S3 speed-optimized functions, branch to a native widening product
when both signed i64 operands fit signed i32. The product fits i64 exactly;
its overflow flag is false. Preserve the ordinary wide intrinsic otherwise.

Keep extensions inside the fast block for instruction selection. Freeze
operands before inserting the guard to avoid new poison-dependent branch UB.
Exclude size-optimized functions, unused overflow flags, statically narrow
operands, constants that never fit, and profiles lacking S3/native multiply.

This is an inactive profitability experiment, not a general speed-parity fix.
Apply after the frozen eighteen-patch mixed-mul chain.

---
